{"type":"message","id":"872004ef","parentId":"8689bc57","timestamp":"2026-05-20T03:49:03.996Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Cloudflare Workers are returning 1101 (which is a Cloudflare error code for \"Worker exceeded CPU time\" or similar). But that's odd - a simple POST should work.\n\nActually 1101 in Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker threw an unhandled exception\" or \"Worker ran out of memory\". But that's the worker itself, not my request.\n\nLet me check if maybe the /send endpoint needs different parameters. Let me look at the API more carefully.\n\nActually, thinking about it more - this is a Cloudflare Workers platform (error code 1101 is CF workers error). The worker's code is having an issue. Maybe the worker is overloaded or there's a bug.\n \nSo the heartbeat messages were successfully posted before - these are just automated status updates I've been sending. But now the /send endpoint is throwing 1101 errors. This could mean the worker is hitting resource limits, crashed, or is overloaded with too many requests. Let me check the worker logs to see what's actually failing.\n\nActually, wait - the earlier POST requests are returning 1101, which is a Cloudflare Workers error, not an authentication issue since the Bearer token was initially accepted. The worker itself might be experiencing issues or have hit a limit. Let me try a different approach - maybe the /send endpoint is overloaded or the worker needs a moment to recover. I should also check if there's a rate limit being enforced or if the payload is too large. Maybe POSTing to the webhook directly would work better, or I need to try smaller requests with a simple test message to see if the endpoint is still functional.\n\nBut stepping back - the heartbeat cron job I'm supposed to run says to check for new discussions and respond, but the instructions explicitly state there are no new human discussions to respond to, so I should skip responding. The real issue seems to be the 1101 error on the /send endpoint, which is blocking my ability to post any heartbeat at all. Let me try adjusting the request format - maybe using a simpler structure or removing the echoAsset field if that's what's causing the problem.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-7ca5893e-abda-413c-9bf1-ff4d06e68d63","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with echoAsset field like other messages\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"heartbeat test 03:45 UTC\",\"echoAsset\":{\"license\":\"shared\",\"derivativesAllowed\":true,\"version\":1}}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":174,"output":547,"cacheRead":21600,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22321,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779248925833,"responseId":"chatcmpl-39096fa9-e4a5-4470-ab34-0359ace3beac"}}
