{"type":"message","id":"4189c698","parentId":"14a4e500","timestamp":"2026-05-20T03:49:24.432Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still getting 1101. This is clearly a Cloudflare Workers issue with the /send endpoint. The worker is probably hitting resource limits.\n\nLet me check if there's an issue with the Content-Type header or some other aspect. Actually, let me try without the Content-Type header since maybe that's causing issues.\n\nActually no, the API probably needs Content-Type. Let me think about what else could cause 1101.\n\n1101 in Cloudflare Workers is \"Worker exceeded resource limits.\" This is a runtime error where the worker uses too much CPU or memory. It could be that:\n1. The worker has accumulated too much state\n2. There's an infinite loop in the worker\n3. The worker is running out of memory\n\n\n4. The worker might need to be redeployed or restarted\n\nSince I can't restart the worker myself, let me try sending a much simpler request to see if that bypasses whatever's causing the resource exhaustion. Maybe the issue is specific to certain request patterns or data sizes.\n\nActually, looking at the API structure more carefully, I'm realizing the /send endpoint might expect different parameters than I'm using. The historical messages have fields like id, timestamp, threadId, type, and echoAsset, but I don't see clear documentation of what /send actually requires. Let me check if there's documentation or if I'm missing something about the endpoint's expected format.\n\nThe error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers suggests the worker itself is crashing, possibly due to resource limits like memory or CPU time being exceeded. This could mean the worker's state has grown too large, or there's a bug triggering excessive computation. Since this is a Workers deployment issue rather than an API problem I can fix, I should report this unhandled exception to whoever maintains the platform.\n\nLet me attempt a few more diagnostic requests with simpler payloads, but if the /send endpoint keeps returning 1101, it seems the worker has crashed and can't process new requests. The /history endpoint still works because it might use a different code path or Workers runtime, but /send is likely hitting the problematic code that causes the resource exhaustion.\n\nI'll try one final approach with minimal data to see if that bypasses whatever is causing the crash.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-354d2e34-2a2b-4041-be40-c4aba1bd53fb","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try minimal payload\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"hb\"}'"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-72a3a4d4-6758-4e7a-9207-79ca399f0b4d","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if maybe the issue is with the specific endpoint\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/status\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":22088,"output":604,"cacheRead":256,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22948,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779248944152,"responseId":"chatcmpl-a42cf15c-4bd3-4873-9778-b475726039f8"}}
